.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA CHANGE-BOOT-IMAGE" "1" "2026-08-26" "0.40.0" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa change-boot-image Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-change-boot-image \- Change the configured ASA boot image for...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa change-boot-image
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the configured ASA boot image for the next reload. The image must already exist on the device, and check mode validates the image path plus containing filesystem access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Filter devices by a Lucene query.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to query.
.TP
\fB\-\-image\-path\fP TEXT
Full ASA image path already present on the device, for example 'disk0:/asa9xxx.bin' or 'boot:/asa9xxx.bin'.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without performing the operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
